# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
# These are authored here and executed on macOS/Linux, where a CRLF shebang
# is not a cosmetic difference -- the kernel reads the interpreter as
# "bash\r" and the script dies with `env: 'bash\r': No such file or
# directory` before its first line runs. That is exactly what happened to
# build-linux.sh on the Ubuntu build box.
*.sh text eol=lf
